                <invention-title lang="de">KONTAKTLINSE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">LENTILLE DE CONTACT</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">CONTACT LENS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A contact lens (100) includes a lens body (1), an electronic component (2), and a circuit structure (3). The lens body (1) includes an optical portion (11) and an annular wearing portion (12) that surrounds the optical portion (11). The annular wearing portion (12) has a layout region (121) having a C-shape and a lower eyelid region (122) that is arranged between two ends of the layout region (121). The electronic component (2) is embedded in the lower eyelid region (122). The circuit structure (3) is embedded in the annular wearing portion (12). The annular wearing portion (12) has a plurality of positioning slots recessed from a surface thereof toward the circuit structure (3), and a bottom side of each of the positioning slots contains a part of the circuit structure (3). An area sum of openings of the positioning slots is equal to or less than 1 % of a sum of surface areas of the lens body (1).</p>
            </abstract>
